the coronavirus pandemic has revealed  europe's vulnerabilities but also our  strengths  we teamed up with scientists and acted  decisively to save lives  together we will emerge stronger  but we cannot expect the future to  become less disruptive  our societies are changing fast and new  trends  or shocks are likely to affect our lives  this is where strategic foresight comes  in to help us  understand the challenges and  opportunities that lie ahead  with strategic foresight we can identify  major trends at play explore alternative  futures  and design forward-looking policies that  make europe more resilient  this will also support our transition to  a green  digital and fair future let's look at  one of the trends to see  how foresight can help us make right  choices today  for a more resilient europe tomorrow  we have entered a green and digital age  radically changing our job market  and the way we work renewable energy  alone  is set to provide some 3 million jobs in  europe by 2050  while robotics is moving from  traditional to smart  powered by artificial intelligence  these trends can greatly improve our  lives but they also  challenge our skills set and may leave  some people behind  strategic foresight helps us to prepare  better  and sooner for such unprecedented shifts  proposing the right responses in  education  employment or social policy  [Music]  good leadership means being decisive in  uncertain times  it also means embracing that uncertainty  taking a strategic approach  to possible futures and shaping the best  way forward  we will now reach out to other  institutions member states  and key stakeholders to look beyond the  horizon  and build our common future together  [Music]
 

